<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carrión de los Condes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carrión de los Condes is a town on the Carrión river in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León. Its name recalls the counts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-gomez">Banu Gómez</a> family who held it in the 10th and 11th centuries, and the infantes de Carrión of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantar-de-mio-cid">Cantar de mio Cid</a>. A major stop on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camino-de-santiago">Way of St James</a>, it has Romanesque churches and the monastery of San Zoilo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carrion-de-los-condes.jpg" alt="Carrión de los Condes" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zarateman · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carri%C3%B3n_de_los_Condes_-_Iglesia_de_Santiago_04.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
